  volume    =  362,
  number    =  1487,
  pages     = "2131--2139",
  abstract  = "The mating system of eastern mosquito fish (Gambusia holbrooki)
               is dominated by male sexual coercion, where all matings are
               forced and females never appear to cooperate and actively avoid
               all attempts. Previous research has shown that male G. holbrooki
               offer a model system for examining the benefits of reversible
